  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Maternal and Child Health Scale Up Proejct in the Upper East Region of Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will document and share learning from promising practices with local government authorities and health authorities as well as development partners to scale up and cover the entire Upper East region. The models will include the pregnancy schools in health centres, bi -monthly airtime credit for mobile phones, water points to project community clinics, Traditional Birth Attendants (TBAs) in basic maternal care, identifying complications and making quick referrals, reproductive health drama to enhance skilled deliveries</narrative>
  </description>
